for these reasons, the court unanimously

1. Dismisses the Government’s preliminary objection;

2. Holds that there has been a violation of Article 1 of Protocol No. 1;

3. Holds that

(a) the respondent State is to pay to the applicant’s heirs who continued the proceedings in his name, within three months, the following sums to be converted into Turkish liras at the rate applicable on the date of payment:

(i) 9,557 (nine thousand five hundred and fifty-seven) US dollars for pecuniary damage; 

(ii) 1,000 (one thousand) US dollars for non-pecuniary damage;

(b) these amounts shall bear simple interest at an annual rate of 5.5% from the expiry of the above-mentioned three months until settlement;

4. Dismisses the remainder of the claim for just satisfaction.

